      "canonicalTopicReview": "The union of the nine printed terms: Fire and gas safety (1.9) with fuel-burning appliances and flues (5.7). Inclusive design of the built environment (1.2). Furniture fitments (10.2). The Ordinary reference taxonomy has no joinery or furniture heading; the term keeps the Wood, Rot & Ventilation association, and 10.2 is declared outside that heading’s crosswalk. Glass and glazing (3.6). Eaves gutters (5.4) at the roof eaves (3.10). Stairs (4.4). The Ordinary reference taxonomy has no stairs heading; the term keeps the Wood, Rot & Ventilation association used for joinery, and 4.4 is declared outside that heading’s crosswalk. Timber and its preservation (10.7); the taxonomy has no node for the structure of a tree. Joints (10.1) and the choice of joint (10.4). The Ordinary reference taxonomy has no joinery heading; the term keeps the Wood, Rot & Ventilation association used for joinery, and 10.1/10.4 are declared outside that heading’s crosswalk. Domestic electrical installation (5.8).",
